***************************
* SET UP THE INITIAL DATA *
***************************

NAME          ODNAMUR

*   Problem :
*   *********

*   A origin-destination matrix estimation problem in the city of Namur.
*   The peculiarity of this problem is to take parking surveys into account
*   as well as traffic counts.

*   The problem is not well conditioned.

*   Source: a true transportation study.  See also
*   M. Bierlaire and Ph.L. Toint,
*   "MEUSE: an origin-destination matrix estimator that exploits structure",
*   Report 93/7, Dept of Maths, FUNDP, Namur, Belgium, EC.

*   SIF input: M. Bierlaire and Ph. Toint, Jan 1993.
*   Updated to improve processing, Pim Heeman, May 2026.

*   classification QBR2-RN-11130-0

* Parameters

* Numberer of parking columns (assumed to be the first)

 IE NPKC                60
 IA NPKC-1    NPKC      -1
 IA NPKC+1    NPKC      1

* Number of centroids

 IE NCENT               106
 IA NCENT-1   NCENT     -1
 RI RNCENT-1  NCENT-1

* Constants

 IE 0                   0
 IE 1                   1
 IA NPKC-1    NPKC      -1

* Gamma : general trust in the countings

 RE GAMMA               1.0000e+04

* Objective for fill-up coefficients

 DO I         0                        NPKC-1
 AE FT(I)               1.0
 OD I

* Inverse of the weights for fill-up coefficients

 DO I         0                        NPKC-1
 AE WFT(I)              1.0
 OD I

* Number of available countings

 IE COUNT               146
 IA COUNT-1   COUNT     -1

* Inverse of the weight on unknow cells

 RE B                   999.999953

